{"seq":35,"at":"2026-10-23","kind":"created","target":{"type":"fact","id":"f28402"},"reason":"New question added to grow the article from five to six facts: Which son of Adam and Eve, born after Cain had murdered Abel, was named by Eve as God's replacement for Abel and became the ancestor of Noah? (answer: Seth), verified against the cited sources.","by":"fact-count-rework","sources":[{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seth"},{"url":"https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Genesis+4%3A25&version=NRSVUE"}],"changes":[{"field":"answerEn","new":"Seth"},{"field":"answerDe","new":"Set"},{"field":"answerRu","new":"Сиф"},{"field":"spans","new":{"en":[473,4],"de":[503,3],"ru":[451,3]}},{"field":"timeline","new":{"kind":"era","start":"-500","end":null,"precision":"century","approx":true,"ongoing":false,"labelEn":"The Book of Genesis reaches its final form in the Persian period (c. 5th century BC)","labelDe":"Das Buch Genesis erhält in persischer Zeit seine endgültige Gestalt (um das 5. Jahrhundert v. Chr.)","labelRu":"Книга Бытия обретает окончательный вид в персидский период (около V века до н. э.)"}},{"field":"source","new":{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seth","title":"Seth – Wikipedia","lang":"en"}}],"hash":"a9511f04f84c"},
